B.ckr=new A.c9("Menus, selects, dropdowns, popovers, date/time and color pickers, autocomplete, context menus and item pickers anchor to their trigger at 768 px and above (flipping above/below and clamping to the viewport so they never leave the screen). Below 768 px they become an edge-anchored bottom sheet \u2014 full width minus 12 px gutters, max height 70%, same content, with a drag handle and tap-outside to dismiss. Tooltips stay anchored on all widths. The choice is the popupAdaptive theme token (anchored | sheet | auto, default auto by width), overridable per component through the adaptive parameter.",null,null)
B.ckt=new A.c9("Every component resolves its style through four legs, from highest to lowest priority: a widget argument, the nearest ComponentTheme in the tree, the app overrides registered at the root, then the token-derived defaults.",null,null)
B.cku=new A.c9("Guideline thresholds: tap-target checks use the mobile tap-target guideline (44/48 px). They are informational for desktop-sized controls (36 px buttons and rows) and are never hidden when they fail.",null,null)
B.ckv=new A.c9("Inline content that appears conditionally \u2014 banners, error messages, chips, list rows \u2014 exits through two primitives. MotionPresence keeps the child mounted while the exit plays, then unmounts it and reports onExited; MotionCollapse adds the height shrink, so siblings slide up underneath. Both accept a MotionSpec override (durations, curves, delay, custom enter and exit builders, disabled for an instant snap) that wins over the theme for that instance only.",null,null)
B.ckw=new A.c9("Density tokens set the default look: compact is the default everywhere (control 32, icon 16, row 32-36), comfortable steps up (control 40, icon 20, row 40-44), and touch targets phone widths automatically (control 48, icon 24, row 48-56). The spacing scale is a 4 px base (4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32) with no ad-hoc values; button and list tile are the reference components that follow these tokens. Override any token per instance or in the theme.",null,null)
B.ckx=new A.c9("Exemptions: none \u2014 every check passes as measured. Purely decorative examples with nothing to announce (no text, no tappable nodes) pass the semantics check vacuously.",null,null)
B.cky=new A.c9("Intensity scales the whole kit from one place: Subtle (0.75x durations, 0.98 press, 4 px enter), Standard (today's values, the default), Expressive (1.5x, 0.94, 12 px) and Custom (explicit press scale, enter offset, duration multiplier and curve choice). The Theme Studio Intensity row picks one; Custom reveals its four numeric rows. Custom legs persist in the theme document, export with Get Code and round-trip through import.",null,null)
B.ckz=new A.c9("Test environment timing: frame times are measured with a stopwatch around pumped frames in the test VM. They compare components relatively; they never predict device frame rates.",null,null)
B.ckA=new A.c9("Right-to-left pumps the preview under Right-to-left direction and checks that it renders with no exception or overflow. Mirroring compares the first Text x in Left-to-right versus Right-to-left: a shift means directional content, equal positions mean a symmetric layout, and no text means not applicable.",null,null)
B.ckB=new A.c9("AnimatedTheme animates ThemeData changes over the duration and curve you pass. Colours tween; layout does not, so a preset or mode switch never reflows the page.",null,null)
B.ckC=new A.c9("Three category legs retime one animation family from a single place, without touching the per-component defaults: overlayEnterDuration and overlayExitDuration (popovers, dialogs, toasts, sheets), stateDuration (toggles, checks, tabs, progress, badge and chip paint, error show and hide), plus the matching overlayEnterCurve, overlayExitCurve and stateCurve. A null leg keeps the component default, so setting a leg only changes the family it names. Every leg scales with the intensity multiplier.",null,null)
B.ckD=new A.c9("Two optional mode-independent tokens make floating surfaces frosted: surfaceOpacity (0..1) multiplies every surface fill, and surfaceBlur (logical px) blurs the backdrop behind it. Cards, dialogs, popovers, menus, tooltips, toasts, sheets, the navigation bar and the scaffold app bar all read them, so one preset change frosts the whole app. The defaults stay opaque (no extra layer), and a component theme value wins over the global when both are set.",null,null)
B.ckE=new A.c9("Test font: the harness pumps previews under the default theme fallback with the test font, so muted text near 4.35 to 4.43 contrast can fail the 4.5 threshold without failing on device fonts.",null,null)
B.ckF=new A.c9("The app leg is the user-owned <name>_theme.dart file the CLI writes next to each component. CLI updates never overwrite it, so your overrides survive an upgrade.",null,null)
B.ckG=new A.c9("Reduced motion collapses everything: when the platform reports MediaQuery.disableAnimations, or the Theme Studio Motion row switches motion.enabled off, every animation resolves to zero duration and its end value, with no tickers or timers running.",null,null)
B.ckH=new A.c9("Every component animation resolves through the motion tokens, read as Theme.of(context).motion. Durations stay in the subtle band \u2014 instant 100 ms, fast 150 ms, base 200 ms, slow 300 ms \u2014 and curves stay restrained, except the spring overshoot used for press-release and pop-in effects. Motion is transform and opacity only, so it never changes layout or a final state.",null,null)
B.ckI=new A.c9("Each component page shows a trust scorecard: accessibility, right-to-left, frame build time and tests. The numbers come from a generated harness run over the component previews; a missing measurement is shown as \u201cNot measured\u201d, never as a pass.",null,null)
B.ckJ=new A.c9("Tokens come in semantic background/foreground pairs. The base token controls the surface colour and the -foreground token controls the text and icons that sit on that surface, so a component never hard-codes a contrast colour.",null,null)
B.ckK=new A.c9("Tests counts registry test cases tagged to the component (file prefix or folder under test/registry/components, plus tags component:<id>). Pass reflects the scorecard harness run at generation time, not the registry suite result.",null,null)
B.ckL=new A.c9("Accessibility checks the preview with the framework guidelines: text contrast (4.5 minimum), labeled tap targets, Android tap targets (48 by 48) and iOS tap targets (44 by 44), plus whether any semantics label, value, hint or tooltip is present.",null,null)
B.ckM=new A.c9("The kit generator runs a generated harness test with the JSON reporter, collects one SCORECARD record per component, counts tests with the analyzer, and writes lib/src/manifests/scorecards.json. The docs generator then emits lib/generated/docs_scorecards.dart from that manifest.",null,null)
B.ckN=new A.c9("Every measured component with its overall badge. Sort by failures to surface the components with the most failing checks.",null,null)
B.ckO=new A.c9("Frame build time pumps 120 frames of 16 ms and reports the p50 and p90 build times in milliseconds. It is labelled \u201cFrame build time \u2014 test environment (relative)\u201d: relative numbers for comparing components, not device performance.",null,null)
